  "title": "State and contents of consciousness",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "3cadf13f-5a64-4753-b797-11086d865468",
      "text": "The state of consciousness is whether and how far a subject is conscious, as in waking, dreaming, deep sleep or anesthesia. The contents of consciousness are what the subject is conscious of, such as a dog, a taste or an itch.",
